[center][size=6][b][color=#b48cff]S3MAPHORE[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][i]Your music. Your rules.[/i][/size]

[b][i]Brought to You by DreamWeave-MP[/i][/b][/center]

[center][size=4][b]Modern, contextual music management for OpenMW.[/b][/size]

No compromises. No bullshit. Your music responds to the world around you.[/center]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]REQUIREMENTS[/color][/center]
[/heading]

[list]
[*][b]OpenMW 0.51 or newer[/b] — [url=https://openmw.org/downloads]Download OpenMW[/url][/*]
[*][b]H3lp Yours3lf[/b] — [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/56417]Download H3lp Yours3lf[/url][/*]
[/list]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]START HERE — WHAT ARE YOU TRYING TO DO?[/color][/center]
[/heading]

[color=#b48cff][b][size=5]I just want S3maphore to manage normal Morrowind music.[/size][/b][/color]

Install S3maphore, enable [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font], and enable [font=Courier New]S3maphore.esp[/font].

[b]You're done.[/b]

Vanilla Explore and Battle music should work immediately.

[color=#b48cff][b][size=5]I installed a music mod that S3maphore supports.[/size][/b][/color]

Install the music mod normally, then enable the matching S3maphore playlist module.

For example, MUSE-style music packs use [font=Courier New]03 Muse Expansion Playlists[/font].

[b]You do not need to edit the music mod or S3maphore's Lua files.[/b]

[color=#b48cff][b][size=5]I want to add my own music.[/size][/b][/color]

[center][b][color=#ffcc66][size=6]PUT THE AUDIO FILES IN THE PLAYLIST'S MUSIC FOLDER.[/size][/color][/b]
[b]There is [color=#9900ff]no Lua step[/color].
There is [color=#9900ff]no filename-registration step[/color].
There is [color=#9900ff]no [i]S3maphore[/i] configuration file[/color] you need to edit.[/b][/center]

S3maphore's playlist modules already contain the rules deciding [i]when[/i] music should play. You supply the music by placing supported audio files in the folder that playlist reads.

The empty [font=Courier New]Music[/font] directories included with S3maphore are intentional drop zones.

The [font=Courier New].gitkeep[/font] files inside them are only placeholders used to preserve empty directories. Ignore them.

For example:

[code]03 Muse Expansion Playlists/
└── Music/
    └── ms/
        └── cell/
            └── hlaalu/
                ├── my-hlaalu-track.mp3
                └── another-track.mp3[/code]

Those tracks are now available to the existing Hlaalu playlist.

[b]You may also provide the same [font=Courier New]Music/...[/font] path from another enabled OpenMW data directory.[/b] The files do not have to be copied directly into S3maphore.

See [b][color=#9900ff][size=4]WHERE TO PUT YOUR MUSIC[/size][/color][/b] below for every existing playlist folder.

[color=#b48cff][size=4][b]I want music to play somewhere S3maphore does not already have a playlist for.[/b][/size][/color]

That is when playlist authoring becomes relevant.

Creating entirely new contextual behavior uses S3maphore's Lua playlist API and is intended for mod authors.

[url=https://dreamweave-mp.github.io/S3ctors-S3cret-St4sh/s3maphore/docs/][b][color=#9900ff]Playlist Author Documentation[/color][/b][/url]

[center][color=#d4d4d8][b]If you are only installing S3maphore, installing supported music packs, or adding songs to existing playlists, you do not need to open or edit a .lua file.[/b][/color][/center]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]INSTALLATION[/color][/center]
[/heading]
[center][size=5][b][color=#ffcc66]Enable 00 Core and S3maphore.esp.[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Everything else in the S3maphore archive is optional.[/b][/center]

[size=4][b]Using an OpenMW mod manager[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]1.[/b] Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/56417]H3lp Yours3lf[/url].[/*]
[*][b]2.[/b] Install S3maphore.[/*]
[*][b]3.[/b] Enable the [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font] data directory.[/*]
[*][b]4.[/b] Enable [font=Courier New]S3maphore.esp[/font] in OpenMW's content list.[/*]
[*][b]5.[/b] Enable only optional modules matching music or content you actually use.[/*]
[*][b]6.[/b] Launch the game.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Installation test:[/b] if normal Explore and Battle music plays, S3maphore Core is installed correctly.

[color=#ffcc66][b]Do not enable every module blindly.[/b][/color]

Optional modules define additional playlists. Many expect music supplied by another mod or by you. If S3maphore cannot find any tracks belonging to one of those playlists, it simply leaves that playlist inactive.

[size=4][b]Manual OpenMW installation[/b][/size]

S3maphore is packaged as several separate OpenMW data directories.

[b]Do not flatten them into Morrowind's [font=Courier New]Data Files[/font] directory.[/b]

Add only the directories you want to [font=Courier New]openmw.cfg[/font].

For example:

[code]data="/path/to/S3maphore/00 Core"
data="/path/to/S3maphore/03 Muse Expansion Playlists"[/code]

Then enable [font=Courier New]S3maphore.esp[/font] from [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font].

[color=#d4d4d8][b]Important:[/b] module numbers are labels, not load-order requirements. They do not need to be enabled in numerical order.[/color]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]WHERE TO PUT YOUR MUSIC[/color][/center]
[/heading]

[center][size=4][b]Adding your own tracks? This is the section you want.[/b][/size]

Choose the existing playlist you want to supply music for and put your audio files in its listed [font=Courier New]Music/...[/font] folder.

[b]For folder-based playlists, every supported audio file in that folder is discovered automatically. Do not add its filename to a Lua file.[/b]

[b]Use the documented folder names [color=#9900ff]exactly[/color]. Do not [color=#9900ff]invent, rename, or reorganize[/color] them.[/b]
[/center]

[spoiler]
[b]00 Core[/b]

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]Music/Explore[/font][/*]
[*][font=Courier New]Music/Battle[/font][/*]
[/list]

