If the context you want [b]does not have an existing playlist[/b], putting music into a newly invented folder will not create one. That is the distinction between:

[list]
[*][b]Adding music to an existing playlist[/b] — put audio files in its folder. No Lua.[/*]
[*][b]Creating a new playlist[/b] — define new contextual behavior using the playlist-author API.[/*]
[/list]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]WHAT S3MAPHORE DOES[/color][/center]
[/heading]

S3maphore replaces OpenMW's built-in music handling with contextual playlists.

Music can react to location, region, cell, faction, enemy, weather, time, tileset, magic effects, or damn near anything else OpenMW exposes to Lua.

For normal users, that complexity is already handled by the installed playlist modules.

You provide music. S3maphore decides when it plays.

For mod authors, the underlying model is:

[list]
[*][b]Playlist[/b] — a collection of tracks with rules for when it may play.[/*]
[*][b]Priority[/b] — decides which valid playlist wins.[/*]
[*][b]Playdeck[/b] — every playlist S3maphore discovers in your OpenMW installation.[/*]
[/list]

When game state changes, S3maphore checks the playdeck and [b]deals[/b] the highest-priority valid playlist.

Battle music is not magic. It is simply a playlist with a combat condition and high priority.

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]MODULES[/color][/center]
[/heading]

Each S3maphore module is an OpenMW data directory containing playlist definitions, music, or both.

[size=4][b]Required[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]00 Core[/font] — the S3maphore engine plus vanilla [font=Courier New]Music/Explore[/font] and [font=Courier New]Music/Battle[/font] playlists. It does not include replacement music.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Major playlist modules[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]01 Tamriel Rebuilt Playlists[/font] — support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/47254]Tamriel Rebuilt - Original Soundtrack[/url].[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]02 Project Cyrodiil Playlists[/font] — support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/55779]Project Cyrodiil Music - Anvil and Sutch[/url].[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]03 Muse Expansion Playlists[/font] — compatibility playlists for MUSE-style music packs, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/51734]Morrow Winds[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/51769]CaptainCreepy Music Pack[/url], and related music mods.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Extended modules[/b][/size]

These are optional and may require a separate music or content mod.

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]04 Vindsvept Solstheim[/font] - support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/53597]Vindsvept Solstheim for Dynamic Music[/url].[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]05 Secrets of the Crystal City[/font] - support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/51932]Secrets of the Crystal City[/url].[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]06 Songbook of the North[/font] - support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/46936]Songbook of the North[/url]. Includes its own music.[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]08 Redguard Music[/font] - support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/56798]Elder Scrolls Adventures Redguard Music for Cyrodiil[/url].[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]09 Nordic Lands[/font][/*]
[*][font=Courier New]10 Inns and Taverns[/font] - support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/55294]Inns and Taverns for Dynamic Music[/url].[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]11 Daggerfall Guild Themes[/font] - support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/53569]Dynamic Music - Daggerfall Guild Themes[/url].[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]14 General Dungeon[/font][/*]
[*][font=Courier New]15 Provincial Music[/font] - support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/46229]Provincial Music[/url].[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]18 Better Music System Redone[/font] - support for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/46312]Better Music System Redone[/url].[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Special-purpose modules[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]07 Starwind Playlists[/font] - for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/48909]Starwind[/url] only.[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]12 BBL Drizzy[/font] - a shitpost playlist pack.[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]16 Bgi Inor[/font] - a shitpost playlist pack with its own music.[/*]
[/list]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]MUSE-STYLE MUSIC PACKS[/color][/center]
[/heading]

S3maphore supports music packs and folder conventions originally designed for MUSE. MUSE itself is an MWSE mod and does not run in OpenMW; you [color=#9900ff]do not need MUSE[/color].

[font=Courier New]03 Muse Expansion Playlists[/font] contains playlist definitions. It does [b]not[/b] include the original music packs.

Install the music pack first, then enable [font=Courier New]03 Muse Expansion Playlists[/font].

[color=#d4d4d8][b]General rule:[/b] if S3maphore finds no tracks for a playlist, it ignores that playlist. Missing music does not fill your game with errors.[/color]

